# Names for addresses. Copy to names.conf (or set names_file in .env). Re-read on change, no restart.
#
# address  name  [type]
#   address: MAC (best for LAN devices: survives an IP change), IP (v4 or v6) or network
#   name:    in quotes if it has spaces
#   type:    pc, phone, nas, server, camera, printer, tv, iot, ap, speaker, vacuum
# A network names every address in it with the host part: "VPN .5".
# Order: MAC, exact IP, the narrowest network, OpenVPN client, /etc/hosts, reverse DNS, maker by MAC.
# Internet addresses may be named too: they show instead of the organization.

# aa:bb:cc:11:22:33     "NAS в кладовке"   nas
# 192.168.1.20          Принтер            printer
# 192.168.1.30          "Камера двор"      camera
# 10.8.0.0/24           VPN                pc
# 203.0.113.10          "Офис Москва"
